nce/argument/1/text\", \"fact\": \"For 0<tau<=1 and real theta>=gamma, tau^theta<=tau^gamma; hence a bound uniform in t of the form K tau^theta ||w||_{H^gamma}^2 gives sup_t||F_n(t;w)||<=K M^2 tau^gamma when ||w||_{H^gamma}<=M.\", \"grounds\": [{\"location\": \"/inference/locals/9\", \"reason\": \"The locally arbitrary step is in (0,1], matching the retained output antecedent.\"}, {\"location\": \"/inference/locals/7\", \"reason\": \"w is the arbitrary mean-zero H^gamma input.\"}, {\"location\": \"/inference/locals/8\", \"reason\": \"M is its retained H^gamma norm bound.\"}, {\"location\": \"/inference/argument/1/text\", \"reason\": \"The numerical exponent comparisons theta>=gamma are explicitly proved here; admissibility is not supplied by these comparisons.\"}], \"justification\": \"tau^theta=tau^gamma tau^(theta-gamma), and 0<tau^(theta-gamma)<=1 (equivalently use log tau<=0). The norm antecedent implies M>=0 and ||w||^2<=M^2; a uniform upper bound remains an upper bound on the supremum. This fact does not establish admissibility of any external loss.\"}]}, \"has_more\": false, \"next_offset\": null}"}}
